  "ingredients": [
    "1 cup almond flour",
    "1 teaspoon all-purpose seasoning (like mrs. dash)",
    "1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon kosher salt",
    "1/4 teaspoon cayenne pepper",
    "2 large egg",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "2 tablespoon heavy whipping cream",
    "1 1/2 cup lard (or other high smoke point oil)",
    "12 ounce chicken sausage"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a mixing bowl add the almond flour and spices.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/low-carb-corndogs-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix all the dry ingredients well so they are completely distributed. Add your eggs to the mixture and scramble them slightly.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/low-carb-corndogs-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add baking powder then some heavy cream to the batter. (If needed to thin it out a bit.) Mix everything well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": null
    },
    {
      "text": "In a saucepan, heat oil to 400F. If you’re not sure whether the oil is ready, you can stick a wooden spoon in and it will start to bubble aggressively.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/low-carb-corndogs-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Get your sausages ready. For this recipe I am using 2 hotdogs and 2 chicken sausages. Dip your hotdog and sausages in the batter before you fry them. Make sure they’re fully coated.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/low-carb-corndogs-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drop your hotdog or sausage into the oil 1 at a time.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/low-carb-corndogs-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let it cook for 2 minutes on one side, then flip it and cook for about 1-2 minutes on the other side.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/low-carb-corndogs-11.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove your hotdogs or sausages from the pan and let it dry on some paper towels. Dish out with some sauces.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-corndogs/#wprm-recipe-50793-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
